message: "If you use myconote-cli in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "myconote-cli: High-performance eukaryotic genome annotation pipeline"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-04-09
authors:
  - family-names: "Narh-Madey"
    given-names: "Benjamin"
    email: "narhmadey@wisc.edu"
    affiliation: "Hittinger Lab, Laboratory of Genetics, University of Wisconsin-Madison"
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/K-nie/myconote-cli"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - genome annotation
  - gene prediction
  - fungi
  - mycology
  - phylogenetics
  - Rust
abstract: >-
  As genome sequencing becomes cheaper and long-read assemblies become
  routine, the bottleneck in genomics has shifted from sequencing to
  annotation. myconote-cli addresses this gap with a high-performance
  annotation pipeline written in Rust, designed for eukaryotic genomes
  with particular strength in fungal biology. It integrates 15
  annotation sources, supports 5 eukaryotic kingdoms and 18 NCBI
  genetic code tables, and takes a genome from raw contigs to
  NCBI-ready submission through a single CLI with built-in validation
  and reproducibility tracking.
